**Refer to the following document to get SNPE SDK: https://developer.qualcomm.com/sites/default/files/docs/snpe/index.html**

**Refer to Main Release Notes for directory structure and Chip code**

## Enabling AI Director and SNPE wrapper

1. In the files: 'Android.mk' & 'iot-media-system.mk' present in the path '<workspace>/vendor/qcom/opensource/iot-media',
   uncomment the below line:
   ```bash
   # AI_DIRECTOR := true
   ```

2. In '<workspace>/vendor/qcom/opensource/iot-media/snpe_wrapper/Android.mk', set the SNPE_SDK variable to the snpe version used.
   Below is the default value set.
   ```bash
   SNPE_SDK := snpe-1.55.0.2958
   ```

2. Extract SNPE SDK archive in '<workspace>/vendor/qcom/opensource/iot-media/snpe_wrapper/snpe_lib/'
   ```bash
   ├── snpe_lib
   │   ├── Android.mk
   │   └── snpe-1.55.0.2958
   ```

3. Once changes are made, build Android images as usual and flash them onto the device

4. After the first boot, perform following steps in order to enable AI Director & SNPE:
   - Run the pre-requisites
     ```bash
     adb root
     adb disable-verity
     adb reboot
     adb wait-for-device
     adb root
     adb remount
     ```

   - Sideload SNPE libraries
     ```bash
     adb push snpe-1.55.0.2958/lib/aarch64-android-clang6.0/* /vendor/lib64/
     adb push snpe-1.55.0.2958/lib/dsp/* /vendor/lib/rfsa/adsp/
     ```

   - For Single camera use-case, run the following commands:
     ```bash
     adb shell "echo outputFormat=0 > /vendor/etc/camera/camxoverridesettings.txt"
     adb shell "echo enableAIDirector=TRUE >> /vendor/etc/camera/camxoverridesettings.txt"
     adb reboot
     ```

   - For 3 camera switch use-case, run the following commands:
     ```bash
     adb shell "echo outputFormat=0 > /vendor/etc/camera/camxoverridesettings.txt"
     adb shell "echo enableAIDirector=TRUE >> /vendor/etc/camera/camxoverridesettings.txt"
     adb shell "echo multiCameraEnable=TRUE >> /vendor/etc/camera/camxoverridesettings.txt"
     adb shell "echo multiCameraEnableFront=TRUE >> /vendor/etc/camera/camxoverridesettings.txt"
     adb shell "echo CameraIdforTeams=8 >> /vendor/etc/camera/camxoverridesettings.txt"
     adb reboot
     ```

5. Once the above steps are done, use the QMedia App to exerise the use-case.
   -  In the App, select camera-id as 0 for either single camera or 3 camera switch use-case.